/package

# Local dev-against-current toggle: `pnpm link ../../libs/flowdrop` writes a
# `overrides: '@flowdrop/flowdrop': link:...` here. Never commit it — the
# committed app always resolves the published package (see README).
# pnpm-lock.yaml is gitignored for the same reason: when generated with the
# link override active it bakes that `overrides:` block into the lockfile,
# which makes Netlify auto-detect pnpm and run a frozen install that fails
# (ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH) since the workspace file isn't deployed.
# The deploy is npm-only: package.json + package-lock.json via `npm ci`.
pnpm-workspace.yaml
pnpm-lock.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*
